    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 7 USER]\ne063\tMy provisional plan is to hear Jonah's revised cut before deciding about postponement.\ne064\tI will compare it with the approved version and write down the exact interpretive difference I still see, if any.\ne065\tFor credit, I will propose equal top-line authorship with detailed role credits below, but I am not sure I can accept that if he still treats structural decisions as his domain.\ne066\tI want to separate the current film from the rules for our next collaboration, and I am not sure they can really be separated.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne067\tListening before deciding prevents an abstract disagreement from hardening around a cut that does not yet exist.\ne068\tYour uncertainty about credit and future authority is also legitimate: a current credit can acknowledge completed work, while the feelings behind it may still determine whether you collaborate again.\ne069\tYou do not need to solve the next project before the showcase, but you may need to avoid using a harmonious credit line as evidence that the underlying process felt mutual.\ne070\tThe revised cut could resolve the edit question and leave the partnership question open.",
